      "statement": "The coordination protocol is a pure decision core with no I/O of its own; a seeded deterministic simulator injects latency, compare-and-swap races, lost responses, clock drift, and crashes at each await point, and checks safety and liveness properties across millions of schedules, with the checkers themselves tested against deliberately broken variants.",
